# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Verification code email — two ways to send it. RECOMMENDED: Resend, an
# HTTP-based email API. It sends over a normal HTTPS request on port 443,
# so it works even on hosts (like Render) whose outbound raw SMTP
# (ports 465/587) is blocked or has no outbound IPv6 route — the cause of
# the "ENETUNREACH ... could not send verification email" error.
#
# 1. Sign up at https://resend.com (free tier is generous for this use case).
# 2. Verify a sending domain (Resend → Domains) for production use, or
#    leave RESEND_FROM_EMAIL blank to use Resend's shared sandbox address
#    (onboarding@resend.dev), which only delivers to the address you
#    signed up to Resend with — fine for testing, not for real users.
# 3. Create an API key (Resend → API Keys) and paste it below.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_KsBo2zCu_Hoeo5Y8gfw81ffYgJseGStNP
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=tdsoft.noreply@gmail.com

# Gmail SMTP — fallback/alternative to Resend above. Used automatically if
# RESEND_API_KEY is blank. Note: on hosts with no outbound IPv6 route,
# earlier versions of this app could fail with ENETUNREACH because
# nodemailer's own DNS resolver ignores the `family` option and can pick
# an IPv6 address for smtp.gmail.com even when told to force IPv4 — this
# is now worked around by resolving the IPv4 address ourselves before
# connecting (see src/utils/email.js), so Gmail SMTP should work again
# too. Still, Resend is the more robust option on hosts that block
# outbound SMTP entirely.
# 1. Turn on 2-Step Verification on the sending Gmail account.
# 2. Generate an App Password: https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
# 3. Paste the 16-character app password below (NOT your normal password).
# If neither RESEND_API_KEY nor these are set, codes are logged to the
# server console instead of emailed — useful for local dev.
GMAIL_USER=tdsoft.noreply@gmail.com
GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=wuwgaileucjhmuvd

# Force a specific provider instead of the RESEND_API_KEY-present ? resend
# : smtp auto-detection above. Leave blank unless you're debugging one
# path specifically. Values: resend | smtp
EMAIL_PROVIDER=smtp

# Seconds an admin must wait before requesting another verification code.
ADMIN_CODE_RESEND_COOLDOWN_SECONDS=30

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Paystack — payments and financial details
# Get these from https://dashboard.paystack.com/#/settings/developers
# Use the test keys (pk_test_/sk_test_) until you're ready to go live.
PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_test_2c0d5ca706241e314883cff6b6a4aef407110c99
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_55bd5db11a16271b3b3f49be5889ea1fe5d5345c
# Small non-refundable-by-default charge (kobo) used to capture a reusable
# card authorization when someone starts a free trial. ₦50 = 5000.
PAYSTACK_CARD_VERIFICATION_KOBO=5000

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IMPORTANT: Do NOT set NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS or NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED.
# This backend always serves plain HTTP (see src/server.js) and never makes
# outbound HTTPS requests that need an extra trusted CA. The only TLS
# connection it ever makes is to Postgres, and that already sets
# `ssl: { rejectUnauthorized: false }` in src/db/pool.js for cloud-hosted
# databases (Render/Neon/Supabase etc.).
#
# A previous version of this file set NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS to a path that
# only existed on one developer's Windows machine
# (".../AppData/Local/mkcert/rootCA.pem"). If you copy this file to `.env`
# and that variable is present but the file doesn't exist on your machine,
# Node will emit TLS/certificate warnings for this process and can produce
# errors like: "self-signed certificate; if the root CA is installed
# locally, try running Node.js with --use-system-ca". Leave this unset.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

